From 5f11497b6839ee17867a19b20cdd64ae8bf54320 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 10:56:23 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Solvers of Trilinos: seventh review, MueLu as an approximate
 solver

- MueLu is also declared as a linear solver of kind APPROXIMATE (one
  V-cycle), for instance for the elastic operator of the Newton-K0 method.
  On the nonlinear beam of tetrahedra of 839,619 unknowns on the GPU, with
  the tangent operator applied without assembly, Newton-K0 takes 6.5
  seconds with MueLu (Jacobi smoother) against 11.2 with one cycle of
  BoomerAMG.
- The processes sharing a GPU are detected by the UUIDs of the devices
  instead of their PCI addresses, the instances of a GPU partitioned by
  MIG having their own UUIDs.
- `use kokkos refactor` is in the master list of MueLu: no exemption
  needed in the check of the parameter names.
- The test resolves once with the factories of MueLu written with Kokkos.
- Documentation: options of the factories written with Kokkos, parameters
  of the Chebyshev smoother, MueLu as a solver.
---
