+of Kokkos Kernels, those of cuSPARSE, the default of Tpetra on CUDA, running
+out of memory on a GPU of 16 GB from a few hundred thousand unknowns).
+Kokkos Kernels reserves up to half the free memory of the GPU for each
+product: several processes using the same GPU (compared by their PCI
+addresses) ran out of memory, and keep the algorithm of cuSPARSE. The
+factories which are not written with :code:`Kokkos` compute the dropping,
+the aggregation and the tentative prolongators on the host (the matrix of
+each level being copied on the host at each full setup, not when the
+hierarchy is reused), and some options only exist in the factories written
+with :code:`Kokkos`: the drop schemes :code:`point-wise`, :code:`cut-drop`
+and the signed distance Laplacians are refused, and :code:`aggregation: use
+blocking`, :code:`aggregation: strength-of-connection: matrix` and
+:code:`measure`, :code:`aggregation: symmetrize graph after dropping` and
+:code:`aggregation: distance laplacian metric` are ignored, unless
+:code:`use kokkos refactor` is set to :code:`true`. On a GPU, the default
+smoother of MueLu (symmetric Gauss-Seidel) is slow: on the beam of 421,443
